    "hints": "To make Vegetable stock paste, please refer to the recipe on Cookidoo®.\n\nFor this recipe, if you don't have any butter simply use a total of 50 g extra virgin olive oil.\n\nYou could add baby spinach leaves to the bottom of the thermal serving bowl before adding in risotto.\n\nRule of thumb for creating your own risotto recipe: for every 100 g risotto rice you will need 250 g liquids (water and wine) combined with stock paste. The maximum quantity of rice that can be cooked at any one time for this recipe is 500 g. Bear in mind adding other ingredients will add volume to the dish, so adjust the rice quantity accordingly."
}



{
    "instructions": [
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Prepare 300 g of coffee with a moka pot, sweeten to taste, and let it cool in a shallow bowl. Separate the egg whites from the yolks."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Insert butterfly. Add egg yolks and half of the sugar to the mixing bowl. Mix 1 min/speed 3 until light and frothy.1 min/40°C//speed 3 1 min//speed 3",
            "annotations": [
                {
                    "type": "TTS",
                    "data": {
                        "speed": "3",
                        "direction": "CCW",
                        "time": 60,
                        "temperature": {
                            "value": "40",
                            "unit": "C"
                        }
                    },
                    "position": {
                        "offset": 115,
                        "length": 20
                    }
                }            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "With the blades running at speed 3, gradually add mascarpone through the hole in the lid until fully incorporated."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Transfer mascarpone mixture to a bowl and set aside. Clean mixing bowl and butterfly thoroughly."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Insert butterfly. Add egg whites to the mixing bowl. Whip 3 min/speed 3.5 until foamy. Gradually add remaining sugar through the hole in the lid."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Whip until stiff peaks form. Gently fold egg whites into mascarpone mixture using a spatula."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Spread a generous spoonful of mascarpone cream on the bottom of a 30x19.5 cm glass dish."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Dip savoiardi briefly in cooled coffee on both sides and arrange in the dish to form the first layer."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Cover savoiardi with more mascarpone cream and smooth the surface."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Repeat the layers with remaining savoiardi and cream. Smooth the top layer of cream."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Transfer remaining cream to a piping bag with a 12 mm plain nozzle and pipe dollops over the entire dish."
        },
        {
            "type": "STEP",
            "text": "Dust with unsweetened cocoa powder and refrigerate for a couple of hours before serving."
        }
    ]
}

